  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A system to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> balls each of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> are connected via massless and unstretchable string. The system is allowed to slip over the edge of a smooth table as shown in figure. Tension on the string between the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>7</mn><mrow><mi>th</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>th</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;ball&nbsp;is _____ &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>6</mn><mrow><mi>th</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup></math> ball just leaves the table.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0075_2a860359b9f4.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 160px;\" /></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "36",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\qt0075_2a860359b9f4.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 160px;\" /></p><p>Acceleration,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Net</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>pulling</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>force</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Total</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mass</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Considering ball&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn></math> as system, tension between ball 7 &amp; 8 can be written as,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>T</mi><mrow><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>m</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>a</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p>"
  }
